From: OpenWrt KDE Plasma Port <openwrt@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Add RDPSND audio playback via PipeWire default sink monitor

Implement per-peer FreeRDP RdpsndServerContext support in KRdp so RDP
clients requesting audio playback receive 48 kHz stereo 16-bit PCM audio
captured from the PipeWire default output monitor. Capture and network
sending are decoupled via a bounded frame queue that drops stale frames
on backlog; teardown stops PipeWire and joins the sender before freeing
the FreeRDP RDPSND context.

